# LabPilot — environment variables template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own keys:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` holds real secrets and is git-ignored — never commit it.
# This file (`.env.example`) holds no secrets and IS committed,
# so anyone cloning the repo knows which keys the project needs.


# --- OpenRouter -------------------------------------------------------------
# Serves fallback chain tiers 1 and 4:
#   tier 1  Nemotron 3 Ultra (:free)   <- primary model
#   tier 4  Ling 3.0 Flash   (:free)
# Also serves the RAG reranker: Llama Nemotron Rerank VL 1B V2 (:free).
#
# Both tiers share ONE daily pool. If the account cap is spent, both fail.
#
# Get a key: https://openrouter.ai/keys
#
# REQUIRED SETTING: in OpenRouter Settings, enable
#   "Allow free endpoints that train on request data"
# Without it, every `:free` model returns an error.
#
# Free tier is roughly 50 requests/day without purchased credits.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=


# --- Google AI Studio (Gemini) ----------------------------------------------
# Serves fallback chain tiers 2 and 3:
#   tier 2  Gemini 3.6 Flash
#   tier 3  Gemini 3.5 Flash
# The high-volume workhorse — free tier allows ~1,500 requests/day.
#
# Get a key: https://aistudio.google.com/api-keys
#
# Both tiers share ONE quota, same as OpenRouter above.
# Note: on the free tier, prompts may be used to improve Google's products.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=


# --- Cerebras Cloud ----------------------------------------------------------
# Serves fallback chain tier 5: gpt-oss-120b (Production).
# Also the development workhorse — use it for bulk test calls while building,
# and keep the small OpenRouter allowance for hard cases.
#
# Get a key: https://cloud.cerebras.ai
#
# Free limits: 2,400 requests/day, but only 5 REQUESTS PER MINUTE.
# The 5 RPM is the limit you will actually hit — plan backoff around it.
# OpenAI-compatible API shape.
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=


# --- Modal --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Modal's MAIN job is serving the fine-tuned model (Gemma 4 + our LoRA adapter).
#
# It also serves fallback chain tier 6 as an emergency backstop:
# Kimi K3, Nemotron Ultra, DeepSeek V4 Pro, DeepSeek V4 Flash.
#
# THIS TIER COSTS MONEY and is NEVER called automatically. When tiers 1-5 all
# fail, the app must warn the user that continuing spends credit and wait for
# an explicit yes. The credit is also needed for the fine-tuned demo, which
# takes priority. Never point development or bulk testing at Modal.
#
# Get a key: https://modal.com
# Leave blank to disable tier 6 — the chain should still work without it.
MODAL_API_KEY=
